WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:25.250
When you've been locked up
for 100 hours,

00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:27.125
chained,
on the brink of death.

00:01:28.292 --> 00:01:29.792
and you've lost
your best friend.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.833
Those 100 hours
feel like 100 years.

00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:39.042
And going outside...

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:41.875
is the biggest freedom
in the world.

00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:46.292
Regardless of being aimed at
by thousands of soldiers.

00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:48.375
Unarmed,

00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:49.833
barefoot,

00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:53.833
with the sun on your face,
surrounded by silence...

00:01:55.042 --> 00:01:56.083
you feel free.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.250
We were sending
a message of hope.

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:07.542
Lisbon was there...

00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:09.583
with us.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:10.750
Walking out of the bank.

00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:14.125
Not at the National Court

00:02:14.208 --> 00:02:16.167
nor in prison,
like everyone thought.

00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:19.333
Colonel Tamayo!

00:02:20.458 --> 00:02:21.958
White flag!

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:26.583
We were telling them...

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.333
that if we were capable
of doing that...

00:02:30.458 --> 00:02:33.042
we would be capable
of doing anything.

00:02:34.042 --> 00:02:37.792
And people began
to believe in miracles.

